{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nSplit from `upbeat-illadvised-springtail` (155c-218b-c128-4700) per operator decision 2026-08-19.\nThat ticket originally carried BOTH the research (which endpoints can move) and the change (moving\nthem). The research must not sit behind the migration's acceptance criteria, so it is filed here\nand springtail is blocked by it.\n\nPydantic AI v2 makes the Responses API the default for `openai:` (the pinned 1.107.2 already\nemits a `PydanticAIDeprecationWarning` saying so on every `openai:` construction). rebar\ncurrently pins Chat Completions explicitly via the `openai-chat:` prefix (the deprecation repair\non `dragonish-sylphic-sheep`). rebar should migrate deliberately, after proving compatibility,\nrather than inherit the semantic change implicitly.\n\n## Scope — evidence only, no migration\nThis ticket does NOT flip any provider to `openai-responses:`. Its product is (a) the capability\nmatrix + production-construction constraints, recorded as a comment on this ticket, and (b) the\ncontract tests that will later prove the migration safe.\n\nEdit-set: ONE new file, `tests/unit/test_openai_responses_contract.py`. No `src/rebar` change —\nfindings about the runtime are recorded on this ticket for `155c` to act on, not patched here.\n\n## Approach\nTwo evidence layers, both against the pinned toolchain (pydantic-ai 1.107.2, this checkout):\n\n1. **Static + probe inventory** of rebar's OpenAI-compatible surface. The rows are exactly the\n   OpenAI-compatible names rebar admits: (i) hosted `openai:` / `openai-chat:` (delegated to\n   pydantic-ai `infer_provider` when no `base_url`), (ii) the custom `base_url` builder\n   `ProviderSession._build_openai` (LMStudio/Ollama/vLLM/LiteLLM recipe, story S4), (iii) the\n   per-candidate `endpoint` override (`ProviderSession.model_for`, task cc33),\n   (iv) `gateway/openai`, and (v) the OpenAI-compatible vendor qualifiers in\n   `KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES` (`deepseek`, `grok`, `xai`, `groq`, `cerebras`, `moonshotai`,\n   `heroku`). Each row is classified Responses-ready / Chat-Completions-only / UNKNOWN from\n   cited evidence: rebar source (file:line), pinned pydantic-ai source/behaviour (which model\n   class `infer_model` constructs per prefix, verified by probe), and live interpreter probes\n   run in this worktree. Vendor-side questions that the pin already decides (pydantic-ai offers\n   no Responses construction path for third-party prefixes) are classified from the pin;\n   anything requiring off-toolchain evidence (e.g. whether a vendor's own API implements\n   `/v1/responses`) is recorded UNKNOWN with the missing evidence named.\n2. **Contract tests** in `tests/unit/test_openai_responses_contract.py`: a stub\n   OpenAI-compatible server behind `httpx.MockTransport` that speaks BOTH wire protocols\n   (`/chat/completions` and `/responses`). Injection mechanism, stated concretely because the\n   `monkeypatch.setattr(httpx, \"AsyncHTTPTransport\", ...)` seam of\n   `test_openai_compatible_provider.py` does NOT reach stock pydantic-ai construction\n   (`create_async_http_client()` builds a bare `AsyncClient`; providers.py:277-283): the test\n   builds one explicit production `OpenAIProvider(base_url=<stub url>, api_key=\"test\",\n   http_client=httpx.AsyncClient(transport=httpx.MockTransport(handler)))` and hands it to\n   `pydantic_ai.models.infer_model(model_string, provider_factory=lambda name: provider)` —\n   the SAME `provider_factory` hook rebar's own `ProviderSession` uses in production\n   (providers.py `model_for`), so `infer_model` still performs the real prefix→model-class\n   dispatch and genuinely constructs `OpenAIChatModel` / `OpenAIResponsesModel`; only the\n   socket inside the explicitly-passed client is faked, and no module attribute is\n   monkeypatched. Tests are parameterized over\n   the two prefixes (`openai-chat:` / `openai-responses:`) so the identical assertions run\n   against both and the parametrize ids ARE the behavioural diff for `155c`. Assertions cover:\n   structured output (Agent `output_type` round-trip), streaming (`run_stream` issues a\n   streaming request and yields text), tool calls (a tool-call turn then a final turn), retry\n   behaviour (a 429 surfaces as `ModelHTTPError` — rebar's OpenAI-compatible builder installs\n   no retrying transport, unlike anthropic's, and the test pins that parity holds across both\n   APIs), and custom-base-URL routing (requests hit the stub `base_url` at the API-specific\n   path).\n\nAlso recorded on the ticket (the production-construction constraints for `155c`): the four\nplaces that today make `openai-responses:` unusable in rebar even though pydantic-ai itself\nconstructs it — `KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES` (src/rebar/llm/config.py) lacks `openai-responses`, so\n`split_provider_qualifier` treats the string as unqualified; `_pydantic_ai_known_providers()`\n(src/rebar/llm/providers.py) derives from `known_model_names()`, which has no\n`openai-responses:` entries, so `is_resolvable` is False and `runner.run()` raises\n`LLMConfigError` (src/rebar/llm/runner.py, the `provider_factory` else-branch);\n`_PROFILE_RESOLVERS` (src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py) has no `openai-responses` key, so\ncapability resolution degrades (`native_structured_output=False`); and the `openai:` →\n`openai-chat:` normalizers (`_pai_model` in src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py and\n`model_classes._resolve_target`) hard-code the Chat pin. Default assumption: these are\n`155c`'s edit-set, not this ticket's.\n\n## Testing\nThe deliverable IS tests. Happy path: every parameterized case passes against the stub for both\nprefixes where behaviour is common. Failure/edge path: the 429-retry case asserts the error\nsurface, and the structured-output case asserts the parse of a well-formed body (the stub also\nlets a later behavioural-diff run mark genuinely divergent cases per-API). Verified by\n`.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_openai_responses_contract.py` plus full `make test`,\n`make lint`, `make typecheck` in this worktree.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A capability-matrix comment on this ticket classifies every row of rebar's\n      OpenAI-compatible surface (hosted openai/openai-chat, custom base_url builder,\n      per-candidate endpoint override, gateway/openai, deepseek, grok, xai, groq, cerebras,\n      moonshotai, heroku) as Responses-ready, Chat-Completions-only, or UNKNOWN, each row with\n      a cited source (rebar file:line, pinned pydantic-ai behaviour, or probe transcript) —\n      checked by reading the comment.\n- [ ] The same comment records the production-construction constraints: each rebar code site\n      that blocks `openai-responses:` today, with file:line — checked by reading the comment\n      against the named sites.\n- [ ] Contract tests exist at `tests/unit/test_openai_responses_contract.py`, construct REAL\n      pydantic-ai models (no mocks of construction; only the transport is stubbed), and assert\n      structured-output, streaming, tool-call, retry, and custom-base-URL behaviour — checked\n      by reading the test file and running it.\n- [ ] The tests are parameterized over `openai-chat:` and `openai-responses:` so re-running\n      them produces a per-case behavioural diff — checked by the parametrize ids in\n      `pytest --collect-only` output.\n- [ ] Any endpoint whose status cannot be established from evidence is recorded UNKNOWN with\n      the specific missing evidence named — checked by reading the matrix comment.\n- [ ] `make test`, `make lint`, `make typecheck` pass in this worktree — checked by running\n      them."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787367686385287001,"uuid":"6e279e70-b07b-459c-a4b0-e6080d8dd4b0"}